  "analysis": {
    "established": [
      "The official owned AVD volume fixture succeeded under ordinary shell UID 2000: one set, volume 5 to 15, first observed at 200 ms. No product volume policy was changed.",
      "The APK entered actual playback; Opus receive/decode counters and reported energy increase, and the existing player reports playing/sound-on without SDK error. These counters do not measure the PCM written to AudioTrack.",
      "The owned AudioFlinger track is active PCM16/stereo/48000 with zero-dB gains and no track or port mute; its output frame count increases. Metadata does not establish nonzero samples at the AudioTrack/HAL boundary.",
      "The full official emulator owns an uncorked/unmuted two-channel 44100 Hz PulseAudio output into the isolated 48000 Hz stereo sink, with all observed volumes at 100 percent. These sample rates can legitimately differ through resampling.",
      "The owned probe records the intended dedicated capture source with zero drops, but sustained 997 Hz remains near zero. An independent stereo parec recording agrees; observed channels do not support cancellation as the explanation."
    ],
    "not_established": [
      "The precise location where nonzero decoded content becomes near-silent output remains unresolved between native playout, AudioTrack/AudioFlinger, Android HAL and emulator output. No production fix is inferred from volume or metadata alone.",
      "AudioFlinger underrun counts increase, but this run does not prove underruns explain near-total silence.",
      "Raw PulseAudio modules JSON was not retained, so exact module identity cannot be reconstructed after CI teardown.",
      "The before_recording and after_recording native UI snapshots contain identical cached counters (1400 packets, 1261920 samples, 0.97 energy and 205 video frames). The old external observer read retained text immediately after opening the panel. Their values do not establish energy growth during the PCM capture window; only the later failure snapshot shows larger cumulative counters. This observation defect is not itself a silence root cause.",
      "The successful volume calibration does not independently validate the whole common output fixture. This run did not include a standalone system-playout positive control, so a shared output/measurement fixture defect is not excluded."
    ],
